<title>THAILAND: Advance Agro plans new 27 bln baht plant.</title>
<headline>Advance Agro plans new 27 bln baht plant.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai pulp and paper firm, Advance Agro Plc, said on Monday it plans to jointly invest with Chinese government to set up a 27 billion baht ($1.04 billion) pulp plant in Thailand.</p>
<p>The plant will have a production capacity of 700,000 tonnes per year, all of which will be exported to China, Advance Agro said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new plant will be located at industrial park in Prachin Buri, 330 kilometres east of Bangkok, it said. ($1=26 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
